### 6.4 Layer 4 — IES Manager (Slot Table with Dedup)

##### [NEW] [servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/ies_manager.h](file:///c:/Users/aiadmin/Desktop/RTX_path_tracing/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/ies_manager.h)
##### [NEW] [servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/ies_manager.cpp](file:///c:/Users/aiadmin/Desktop/RTX_path_tracing/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/ies_manager.cpp)

```cpp
class IESManager {
public:
    // Returns slot index. Content is hashed for dedup.
    int add_ies(const String &p_content);
    int add_ies_from_file(const String &p_filepath);

    // Decrement reference count. Marks for GPU re-upload when reaching 0.
    void remove_ies(int p_slot);

    // Upload all active IES data to GPU SSBO.
    void device_update(RenderingDevice *p_rd, RID &r_ies_buffer);

    bool is_dirty() const { return needs_update; }

private:
    struct IESSlot {
        IESFile ies;
        uint32_t hash = 0;
        int users = 0;
    };

    LocalVector<IESSlot> slots;
    Mutex mutex;
    bool needs_update = false;
};
```

**Design decisions (matching Cycles):**

| Feature | Implementation |
|---------|---------------|
| **Hash dedup** | `String::hash()` on raw content — identical IES text shares one slot |
| **Ref counting** | `users` field incremented on `add_ies`, decremented on `remove_ies` |
| **Slot recycling** | Empty slots (users==0, hash==0) reused before appending |
| **Thread safety** | All operations protected by `Mutex` |
| **Dirty flag** | Set on any add/remove; cleared after GPU upload |

