### 6.6 Layer 6 — Shader Evaluation

##### [NEW] [raytracing/ies_lookup_inc.glsl](file:///c:/Users/aiadmin/Desktop/RTX_path_tracing/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/raytracing/ies_lookup_inc.glsl)

Port of Cycles' `kernel/util/ies.h` — bicubic interpolation in spherical coordinates:

```glsl
// Bicubic IES lookup.
// Returns intensity multiplier for the given direction.
float ies_lookup(int slot, vec3 direction) {
    if (slot < 0) return 1.0; // No IES profile, isotropic fallback

    int ofs = floatBitsToInt(ies_data[slot]);
    if (ofs < 0) return 1.0; // Invalid slot

    // Compute spherical coordinates from direction
    vec3 d = normalize(direction);
    float v_angle = acos(clamp(-d.y, -1.0, 1.0));   // Vertical: 0 at top (Y-up)
    float h_angle = atan(d.x, d.z) + PI;             // Horizontal: 0..2π

    // Read grid dimensions
    int h_num = floatBitsToInt(ies_data[ofs]);
    int v_num = floatBitsToInt(ies_data[ofs + 1]);

    // ... bicubic interpolation (4x4 grid sampling) ...
    // Full implementation mirrors kernel_ies_interp() from Cycles
    // with pole wrapping and wraparound for full 360° horizontal

    return max(result, 0.0);
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> Our engine uses **Y-up** coordinates whereas Blender Cycles uses **Z-up**. The vertical angle computation changes from `acos(-z)` to `acos(-y)`, and horizontal uses `atan(x, z)` instead of `atan(x, y)`.

